TODO

Done
  * Packaging (0.1.0): GNU autotools (configure.ac + Makefile.am), install
    layout (host binaries under $(libexecdir)/v7unix, v7cc/v7as/v7ld symlinks
    in $(bindir), target runtime in $(libdir)/v7unix, manpages in a v7unix
    section), and the dist/ template tree + README.distributions for 10
    distributions.
  * froot (the minimal self-hosting root): tools/mkfroot.sh + `make froot`,
    verified by tools/selfhost.sh — compiles the toolchain subset
    (cc/as/ld + friends) from orig/ with only the pieces inside froot.
  * make, yacc, sh ported to modern/ (modern/usr/src/cmd/{make,yacc,sh}).
  * Basic utilities ported to modern/: rm, cp, cmp, mv.
  * adb source modernized to pcc99/ (target-resident; never a host binary).
  * V7 reference binaries shipped for byte-comparison (orig/bin, orig/lib).

Remaining
  * Manifests: replace mkfroot.sh's hardcoded file list with two manifest
    files, one path per line, so we know what goes into froot/ —
      froot.toolchain  the subset that rebuilds the toolchain itself
      froot.wholetree  everything needed to build the whole tree
    mkfroot.sh already takes the scope (--scope / toolchain|whole) and seed
    (c17=modern / c99=pcc99); the manifests make the per-scope file lists data
    instead of shell.
  * Whole-tree scope: port the rest of the utilities so the wholetree manifest
    is complete and the full /usr/src tree builds self-hosted, not just the
    toolchain subset:
    Step 1 — toolchain, pure C: touch, ls, diff.
    Step 3 — whole tree, pure C: lex, sed, tar, tp, grep, ln, mkdir, chmod,
      chown, cat, echo, pr, strip, size, install, du.
    Step 4 — whole tree, assembly: factor, primes, bas, roff, standalone.
  * Basic build utilities (V7 behavior, not host equivalents): touch, ls, diff,
    ln, mkdir, chmod, chown, cat, echo, pr.
  * libc.a byte-identity: the modern-built lib/libc.a must reproduce
    orig/lib/libc.a byte-for-byte; it currently differs (1071 bytes, first at
    the archive header).  pcc99/lib/libc.a is not expected to match.
  * lex: not needed for the toolchain itself (orig/ has no .l files); needed
    for the whole tree (awk + struct) — see CROSSCOMPILE.md §5.
  * Headers: install V7 target headers under $(includedir)/v7unix.
  * Port mkfs and fsck to the modern host (kept in this repo; filsys depends
    on it for them).

Notes
  * Scope rule: port to modern/ (host C) only what *executes* on the host.
    crt0.o / fcrt0.o / mcrt0.o / fmcrt0.o / libc.a are linked, never run
    standalone, and stay as PDP-11 assembler/objects.
